= Wrangel Leaves Crimea

In November 1920, General Wrangel's army, the last of the White forces, evacuated the Crimea in the face of the Red Army's attack. Over 140,000 soldiers and civilians left on the ships of the French navy. The Civil War, in the sense in which it was understood, is over.

There is no longer an outside enemy to justify the repression. The party's leaders have been sent abroad: Martov to Berlin, ill, with his Socialist Courier, and Abramovich after him. Those who remain, Dan and the Central Committee, are to say whether the soviets can be reformed from the inside.
